Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: SAX2.c
Line: 2580
Function: xmlSAX2Text
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: When appending to an existing text node, if newSize >= capacity and newSize > INT_MAX/2, capacity is set to INT_MAX. This ensures capacity >= newSize but not capacity > newSize. The subsequent write content[newSize] = 0 can therefore write one byte past the allocated buffer when newSize == INT_MAX (possible with XML_PARSE_HUGE), causing a 1-byte heap overflow.

